 {"skill": "svg-authoring", "decision": "admitted", "date": "2026-10-11", "family": "design / asset authoring. It sits between `iconography` (the incumbent set answers first) and `image-generation` (a raster), and beside `logo-generation`, `canvas-design` and `wireframe`, which all produce hand-authored SVG and route into it rather than restating it.", "capability": "The procedure for writing or editing an SVG by hand, and the status vocabulary that binds a claim to evidence: read the delivery mode, classify the asset, write with the invariants, run the static witness, run the engine witness, look, and report `verified` only against a render manifest whose digest equals the delivered file's. Raster-to-vector is a named branch with a measured procedure rather than a look. Six lanes produced hand-authored SVG and none of them had any of this.", "why_not_extend": "Measured against the overlap scan, not asserted: no existing skill holds a hand-authored-SVG procedure, and the six producing lanes sit in three packs — `iconography`, `wireframe` and `design-intelligence` in frontend-design, `logo-generation` in ai-image, `canvas-design` in ai-video — plus one guideline. A reference file under any one of them is unreachable from the other two packs, while `packs:` takes a list, so the owner reaches all of them and a reference cannot. Recorded as decision E2 of road-to-svg-with-a-witness.", "why_not_a_guideline": "A guideline is read; this is executed. Its steps invoke two checkers and bind a status word to one of their outputs — `verified` requires a render manifest whose recorded digest equals the delivered file's digest on disk, which is a procedure with a falsifiable outcome rather than advice. The prose half of the same roadmap DID go to guidelines and authorities: the motion mechanisms to fe-design's § Motion, the ARIA rows to the accessibility corpus, the render-security sinks to that skill. Only the procedure is here.", "visibility": "Routed, not browsed. It ships `evals/triggers.json` with six should-trigger and six should-not-trigger queries whose near-misses are exactly the neighbours above, and the six lanes each carry a one-line pointer into it. The description is 130 characters and names the six jobs plus the two checks, so a host that shows only descriptions still routes it. Its catalogue line costs 32 tokens, paid back in the same change by trimming four lane descriptions: the per-spawn preamble payload measures 135,975 against a measured ceiling of 135,980.", "roadmap": "road-to-svg-with-a-witness", "estate_cost": "skill_count 299 -> 300, claimed with estate_growth_exempt in the roadmap's own frontmatter; skill_description_tokens 11,460 -> 11,456, a net REDUCTION because the four lane descriptions were compressed by more than the new one costs."}
+{"skill": "type-design", "decision": "admitted", "date": "2026-10-18", "family": "design / asset authoring. It sits beside `typography-system` (choosing and pairing existing fonts), `svg-authoring` (one vector asset, whose trace-to-measure and counter rule it reuses), `logo-generation` and `brand-identity` (where a wordmark is born), and `iconography` (an icon font from an existing set). Each of those routes \"make this a font\" into it rather than restating it.", "capability": "Building an original font as a constructed system: a rights gate before any trace, a license that is asked and never stamped, no freehand outlines, a font-spec.yaml that code builds every outline from, a construction order through derivation chains, spacing before kerning, peer-side gates with thresholds (outline hygiene, vertical metrics, stem consistency by ray-cast, fidelity IoU), and a rendered proof read through the asset witness. No skill under src/ named or carried any of it (0 hits for a font compiler, a UFO library or a tracer at main@17f028941).", "why_not_extend": "Decision A1 of road-to-type-with-a-witness: a reference under svg-authoring would put a twelve-step pipeline behind a one-asset trigger, and the neighbours sit in different packs (typography-system and svg-authoring in frontend-design, logo-generation in ai-image, brand-identity in brand), so a reference inside one of them is unreachable from the others. A1's recorded fallback was a reference file if no same-change payload reduction could be found; one was found, so it did not fire.", "why_not_a_guideline": "A guideline is read; this is executed. Its steps run a pinned toolchain, gate on measured thresholds and bind the maturity label `validated-static` to every gate being green and the witness reading `loaded` - a procedure with a falsifiable outcome, not advice. The delivery prose half went to the delivery owner instead: the metric-matched fallback derivation lives in docs/guidelines/design-asset-discipline.md and gates.md points at it.", "visibility": "Routed, not browsed. It ships evals/triggers.json with six should-trigger and five should-not-trigger queries whose near-misses are the four neighbours, and four neighbours carry a one-line pointer into it. The description is 149 characters. Its catalogue line is paid back in the same change by removing two See-also bullets that duplicated a link already in the same rule body: the per-spawn preamble payload measures 135,880 against a ceiling of 135,907.", "roadmap": "road-to-type-with-a-witness", "estate_cost": "skill_count 300 -> 301 and skill_description_tokens 11,455 -> 11,489, both claimed with estate_growth_exempt in the roadmap's own frontmatter; the per-spawn preamble payload falls by 27 tokens."}
